# Timesheet context

The billables `daily` skill reads this file every run. It's your source of truth for
*who's who* and *which client each activity belongs to*. Keep only confirmed facts;
the skill will propose additions when it learns something new — review and merge
those additions rather than letting them accumulate elsewhere.

You can hand-edit this file at any time. The skill never overwrites it without
showing you the diff first.

Keep it lean: only *your* facts belong here — generic heuristics live in the skill
itself, and the skill checks this file against a size budget (default 14,000 bytes,
see SKILL.md Step 11) after every edit and compacts when it's exceeded.

---

## Preferences

Override the skill's defaults here. Omit any line you're happy with as default.

Your timezone is *not* here: it is machine configuration, set once at install
(`/plugin configure billables` → `TIMESHEET_TIMEZONE`), so it can't drift out of step with
a second workspace. Everything below is a judgement call about *your* working style, which
is why it lives with your facts rather than in a shipped script.

- **AFK threshold for a real break**: `1050s` (17.5 min) — shorter AFK folds into work
  <!-- afk_blocks --afk-threshold -->
- **Substantive activity floor**: `120s` — a shorter not-afk run is a flicker, not work
  <!-- afk_blocks --solid; lower it if your real work arrives in short bursts -->
- **End-of-day blip gap**: `600s` — this long after the last substantive activity, the
  day's last moment is a mouse nudge, not work  <!-- afk_blocks --blip-gap -->
- **Smallest uncovered stretch worth flagging**: `900s` (15 min) — below this, activity
  the proposed blocks miss is rounding  <!-- afk_blocks --min-uncovered -->
- **Active / thin bands**: at or above `0.7` active_ratio a stretch is billable, below
  `0.4` it is mostly idle  <!-- afk_blocks --active-band / --thin-band -->
- **Timeline noise floor**: `5s` — shorter window events are tab-switch noise
  <!-- activity_timeline --noise-floor -->
- **Timeline gap fold**: `60s` — a shorter gap doesn't break a span in two
  <!-- activity_timeline --gap-fold -->
- **Smallest span the timeline prints**: `3.0 min` — shorter ones are hidden from the text
  view but still counted in the rollup  <!-- activity_timeline --min-span -->
- **Minimum billable block**: `0.25 hr` — nothing shorter is posted as its own entry
  <!-- no flag: the model applies this when it drafts, per references/output-format.md -->
- **Lunch detection window**: `11:30`–`14:30` local — longest AFK in here is lunch
- **Work-hours window for AW rendering**: `06:00`–`20:00` local
- **Default Harvest task for client work**: `Gen - Development/Configuration`
- **Default Harvest task for internal/admin time**: `Meeting - Standup Meetings`
- **Display name in window titles**: `<YourFirstName>` (used by Edge profile signal — e.g. titles ending `… - <Profile> - <YourFirstName> - Microsoft Edge`)

Each `<!-- ... -->` names the flag the skill passes when you change the value beside it.
Changing a number here is the supported way to retune the skill; editing the constant in a
shipped script is not — an update overwrites it.

## AW buckets

(The skill caches these after first discovery so subsequent runs skip the buckets endpoint.)

- Hostname suffix: `<YOUR-MACHINE-NAME>`  <!-- e.g. WS-113359 -->
- Window: `aw-watcher-window_<HOST>`
- AFK: `aw-watcher-afk_<HOST>`
- Web (Firefox): `aw-watcher-web-firefox_<HOST>`
- Web (Edge/Chrome): `aw-watcher-web-chrome_<HOST>`
- VS Code: `aw-watcher-vscode_<HOST>` (optional)

